{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB14512 - MONDO_11292",
  "verbalization": "Mometasone Furoate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Dermatitis, Atopic through a chain of indications that connect it to other conditions and their respective treatments. The evidence suggests that Mometasone Furoate is associated with Contact Dermatitis and Granuloma Annulare, both of which are linked to Dermatitis, Atopic via their respective treatments. This implies a potential pathway where Mometasone Furoate may influence the development or progression of Atopic Dermatitis through indirect mechanisms, possibly by modulating inflammatory responses or skin barrier function. The recurring association with Dermatitis, Atopic highlights a possible role in the broader context of atopic dermatitis pathophysiology, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a network of interactions that may contribute to the manifestation of Atopic Dermatitis, but further research is needed to elucidate the precise causal relationships.",
